The synthetic path tests found a material issue: when one 1-minute candle crosses both breakout stops, ML4T fills both orders before the strategy can cancel the opposite stop. The callback cannot enforce OCO after the event. This is now a recorded failed test, and I’m checking the native broker’s contingent-order support before deciding whether the engine can represent the rule or the result must remain unresolved.
