Executed the one-bar Dukascopy Phases 5–7 and recorded the results in the [audit report](</home/quant/dev/quant/quant-research/docs/audit/one_bar_dukascopy_phase567_20261011.md>). The corrected historical baseline finished before the new runs; its wrapper exit code remains unexplained.

The final native ML4T replays produced **$246,630.04** at zero cost and **$166,521.58** with $2.50 commission and 0.25 adverse points per fill. Independent review reconciled both ledgers to equity and reproduced daily Sharpe and drawdown. The six synthetic tests pass, including tests that document the unresolved same-minute OCO failure.

**Decision: INCONCLUSIVE.** Gap-fill effects, the OCO race, the unqualified CFD proxy, and the negative 2026 block prevent a robust strategy claim. The protected post–July 14 data was not read.

Skipped 2×/3× cost, delayed-fill, and placebo runs; no confidence intervals were computed. Main risk: stop-price gap fills materially affect PnL. The attached run’s exit code was unavailable.
